# EAP-TLS against a stock strongSwan, which caps its TLS stack at 1.2
# (`version_max = 1.2`, /etc/strongswan.d/charon.conf) and implements no
# RFC 7627 Extended Master Secret: `extended_master_secret` appears in
# strongSwan 5.9.14 only as a name in a log table, never in tls_peer.c or
# tls_server.c.
#
# RFC 5216 Section 2.3 defines the EAP-TLS MSK as a crypto/tls
# ExportKeyingMaterial result, and Go refuses that export when the session is
# below TLS 1.3 AND did not negotiate RFC 7627 (crypto/tls conn.go: `c.vers !=
# VersionTLS13 && !c.extMasterSecret`). Both halves hold here, so ze cannot
# authenticate this peer without opting in.
#
# It is set HERE, per scenario, rather than as a //go:debug line in
# cmd/ze/main.go, so a shipped ze stays fail-closed and an operator who needs it
# opts in knowingly (Thomas, 2026-08-01). Scenario 06-eap-tls13 is the same
# exchange over TLS 1.3 and carries no ze-env file at all, which is what proves
# the TLS 1.3 path needs no weakening.
GODEBUG=tlsunsafeekm=1
